# ==== T-FMT-D (R41) fill-pack matrix — LIST KIND = TUPLE literal.
#
# SUBJECT: this fixture asserts `gg fmt` OUTPUT (byte-for-byte, in
# `fmt_fill_pack_tuple_literal_kind`) — a bulk `gg fmt` sweep MUST EXCLUDE it.
#
# Emit site: the `Expr::TupleLiteral` arm of `format_expr` -> the delimited-list
# chokepoint `emit_delimited_list("(", ")", ..)` -> `doc::surround_fill`.
#
# Axis cell claim (Core #12 — `list kind x fit` for the TUPLE-LITERAL kind ONLY):
#   tu_empty  empty              `()`
#   tu_flat   fits-flat          one line, no trailing comma
#   tu_fill   needs-fill         greedy packing at the block continuation indent
#   tu_over   single-over-width  a TWO-element tuple, deliberately: the
#                                one-element spelling `(x,)` never reaches the
#                                packer at all — it does not even go through the
#                                delimited-list chokepoint, because the trailing
#                                comma IS the tuple, so that branch emits
#                                `(` expr `,)` directly and consults the comment
#                                side-table itself. A single-element over-width
#                                tuple would therefore sample nothing here.
#
# RED source per row: tu_fill / tu_over are TRUE pre-fix REDs (one element per
# line with a trailing comma and a bare `)`). tu_empty / tu_flat are invariant —
# break-and-restore them by lowering `doc::MAX_WIDTH`.
void tu_empty():
    auto z = ()

void tu_flat():
    auto a = (111111, 222222, 333333)

void tu_fill():
    auto b = (111111, 222222, 333333, 444444, 555555, 666666, 777777, 888888, 999999, 101010, 111011, 121212, 131313)

void tu_over():
    auto c = (aSingleTupleElementIdentifierWhoseRenderedWidthAloneExceedsTheEntireLineWidthBudgetOfTheGorgetFormatter, 7)
